{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":488224,"name":"aiaje com","username":"aiaje_com","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/919ad9/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:16:05.571Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Windows, Grok Bot’s in-app updater downloads a new installer, then refuses to install it. Settings show: “다운로드한 업데이트를 확인할 수 없어 설치되지 않았어요” (The downloaded update could not be verified, so it was not installed.)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe app version stays on the old build. Seen on 0.36.0 stuck while 0.39.0 was current (2026-09-04), and again on 0.44.0 stuck while 0.47.0 was current (2026-09-10). %LOCALAPPDATA%\\sand-updater\\installer.exe remains the already-installed version.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe official Setup.exe from \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/download/bot\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCursor · Download Grok Bot\u003c/a\u003e has Authenticode status Valid and signer “Anysphere, Inc.” and installs correctly when run manually (Setup.exe /S).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is desktop app update, not Agent Computer image update/reset.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInstall Grok Bot on Windows x64 (stable track, auto-update on).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWait until a newer stable is published on the official Grok Bot download page.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Settings → Updates → Check for Updates (or wait for auto-update).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDownload progress appears, then the unverified-install error. App FileVersion does not change.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter a successful download, the signed installer should be staged and applied on quit/restart, matching the version on the download page.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.47.0 (Windows x64), currently installed after a manual official Setup.exe. Previously stuck at 0.36.0 then 0.44.0. Windows 11 10.0.26200.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e0.47.0 app.asar still contains the same probe: Get-AuthenticodeSignature via powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command, then JSON.parse of stdout, requiring status === “Valid” and signer in [“Anysphere, Inc.”, “Anysphere”]. Failure kind: installer_signature_invalid (UI id VZlSAx). On failure the downloaded file is deleted.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnysphere installers use short-lived Microsoft ID Verified / Azure Trusted Signing certificates (~3 days) plus a timestamp. Get-AuthenticodeSignature from an interactive PowerShell session still returns Valid after NotAfter because of the timestamp. The in-app Electron execFile(“powershell.exe”, …, { windowsHide: true }) path can still fail (unreadable JSON, status not exactly Valid, unexpected SimpleName), which matches “download happened, install never started”.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSuggested fix: verify with WinVerifyTrust / timestamp-aware Authenticode without parsing PowerShell JSON; do not delete a just-downloaded installer on a probe parse error; don’t treat Agent Computer reset as the recovery path for this desktop-app failure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOfficial installer that applied cleanly (0.47.0):\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca href=\"https://downloads.cursor.com/grokbot/stable/win32-x64/0.47.0/Grok_Bot_0.47.0_Setup.exe\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://downloads.cursor.com/grokbot/stable/win32-x64/0.47.0/Grok_Bot_0.47.0_Setup.exe\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488224-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488224-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-10T15:16:15.141Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":1,"readers_count":0,"score":25.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":171265,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-windows-in-app-update-downloads-then-fails-authenticode-probe-installer-signature-invalid","display_username":"aiaje com","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url"